course: dictionary
lesson: 3309
title: EU, eu and eu
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The same spelling can mean different things. Capital letters, EU, are an abbreviation for the European Union, a group of many European countries that work together on trade, travel, laws and money.
explain: «Ukraine applied to join the EU in February 2022.» Here EU means the European Union. Ukraine is a candidate, not yet a member, so the sentence shows that joining takes time.
explain: Small «eu» can be a French or Portuguese word. In French, «J'ai eu dix ans hier!» means «I turned ten yesterday!», because «eu» is part of the past tense of «avoir» (to have). In Portuguese, «eu» means «I». The words around it tell you which language you are reading.
fact: EU (capital letters) is an abbreviation for the European Union, a group of many European countries.
fact: Many EU countries share the euro, a common money. The UK left the EU, but Ireland is still a member.
fact: In French, «eu» is the past form of «avoir»: «j'ai eu» means «I had», and it sounds like «oo» said with rounded lips.
fact: In Portuguese, «eu» means «I».
fact: Check the context first: lessons about countries and money mean EU, while sentences about having or being mean French or Portuguese «eu».
exercise: «Ukraine applied to join the EU in February 2022.» What does EU stand for? | *European Union | Extra Unit | Every Unicorn | Easy Upgrade
exercise: «J'ai eu dix ans hier!» In French, what does «eu» mean here? | You have | *I had | I am | We will be
exercise: In Portuguese, «eu» means which English word? | You | They | *I | We
test: «Eu sou aluno.» In Portuguese, what does «eu» mean in this sentence? | We are pupils | They are pupils | You are a pupil | *I am a pupil
test: Which country left the EU? | Ireland | *The UK | France | Germany
exam: In «J'ai eu peur», meaning «I was scared», what does «eu» show? | Are | Am | *Had | Will
